{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>And the slope of the streams.</b> The Targum renders אֶשֶׁד as שֶׁפֶךְ — the spill of the streams, where the blood of the Amorites was spilled there. For they would hide there, because the mountains were high and the streambed deep and narrow, and the mountains close to each other — a person standing on the mountain from this side could speak with his fellow on that mountain — and the road passed through the streambed. The Amorites said: When Israel enter the land through the streambed to cross, we will come out from the caves in the mountains above them and kill them with arrows and catapult stones. Now those clefts were in the mountain on the side of Moab, and in the mountain on the side of the Amorites, opposite those clefts, were protrusions like horns and breasts jutting outward. When Israel came to cross, the mountain of the land of Israel trembled like a maidservant going out to greet her mistress, and drew near to the mountain of Moab, and those breasts entered into those clefts and killed them. And this is 'which inclined to settle at Ar' — that the mountain inclined from its place and drew near to the side of Moab and clung to it. And this is 'and it leaned against the border of Moab' (Numbers 21:13). (Tanhuma; Berakhot 54)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:59.002064834Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}